# Secrets — never committed (00_START_HERE rule 5)
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.keystore
*.jks
google-services.json
serviceAccountKey.json

# Node
node_modules/
dist/
*.tsbuildinfo
npm-debug.log*

# Build artifacts
apk/*.apk
app/dist/
# ⚠ The Android platform is NOT generated — it is hand-customised (manifest
# permissions, six native plugin classes, google-services.json) and lives ONLY at
# C:\dev\eve\app\android, untracked. A clone/worktree gets nothing here. NEVER run
# `npx cap add android` to repopulate it — that overwrites it with a blank template
# and silently strips the mic, SMS and push. COPY the directory out of production
# instead. `npx cap sync android` is safe. See RUNBOOK_push_and_apk.md Part B.
app/android/

# Runtime data (device push tokens — mildly sensitive; deliverables regenerate
# and now also live in the DB). Her wardrobe IS re-included: those renders must
# ship to the host or she has no closet. Negation needs the /* form — you
# cannot re-include a file whose parent DIRECTORY is excluded.
brain/data/*
!brain/data/wardrobe/
brain/data/wardrobe-state.json

# Firebase / signing (never commit)
*service-account*.json
keystore.properties
*.jks

# OS
Thumbs.db
.DS_Store

# Her closet lives in Supabase Storage (scripts/sync-wardrobe.mjs), not git:
# keeps the repo small, deploys fast, and adding a look needs no redeploy.
# The /* form (not the bare dir) so specific data files can be re-included;
# wardrobe stays OUT (Supabase). EVE's fleet manifest DOES ship — she reads it
# at runtime (fleet.ts).
brain/data/*
!brain/data/fleet-roster.json
brain/*.log
brain/prompts/*.bak

# Built APKs carry VITE_BRAIN_TOKEN baked into the JS bundle in plaintext.
# Anyone holding the file holds the brain token. Never commit one.
apk/
*.apk
